  <h1>Record Audio in the Equalizer: Recording Source, Settings &amp; Download in the 19-Band EQ Pro</h1>

  <div class="blog-meta">
    <span class="blog-meta-badge">How-to</span>
    <span>October 4, 2026</span>
    <span>· 7 min read</span>
  </div>

  <p>
    Dialing in the equalizer and compressor is one half of the job; keeping the result as a file is the other. That is why the KodiniTools 19-Band EQ Pro does not record the original file but the fully processed signal: whatever you hear ends up in the recording exactly like that. The source can be the playlist, a microphone, a line-in or your PC's own sound. This guide shows how to choose the recording source, which settings are available and how the download works.
  </p>

